/target
/tools/probes
/tools/__pycache__
**/node_modules
**/target
*.wasm
# Staged build outputs: the page fetches these, and they are rebuilt by the scripts that
# sit next to them. The image is 16 MiB, which is the reason it is named explicitly.
tools/wasm-browser/build/

# The published demo is the one place build output *is* committed: GitHub Pages serves `docs/`
# straight out of the repository, so `just publish-wasm` stages the artifacts there on purpose
# ("Publishing it" in `tools/wasm-browser/README.md`). The negation has to come after the
# `*.wasm` rule above, and the boot image — 16 MiB — is not ignored anywhere, so it goes in with
# them.
!docs/build/*.wasm
